{
  "info": {
    "name": "AI Gateway - azure-managed-identity policy",
    "_postman_id": "c7a3b9e1-2f4d-4a8b-9e1a-azuremanagedid",
    "description": "End-to-end test collection for the azure-managed-identity dev policy - User-Assigned Managed Identity auth via Azure IMDS, with the same Redis-backed token cache design as the oauth2 policy.\n\nCompanion to gateway/dev-policies/azure-managed-identity/TESTING.md - read that doc for the full narrative; this collection is the same flows as importable requests.\n\nUnlike oauth2, this policy is attached via the generic policies list (not the typed upstream.auth field) - matching how aws-authentication is attached today.\n\nPrerequisites before running any folder here:\n1. Start mock-azure-imds (see TESTING.md Part A):\n   cd gateway/dev-policies/azure-managed-identity/mocks/mock-azure-imds && GOWORK=off go run .\n2. Start mock-ai-backend (shared with the oauth2 policy's harness, unchanged):\n   cd gateway/dev-policies/upstream-oauth2-authentication/mocks/mock-ai-backend && GOWORK=off go run .\n3. Build the gateway with the policy included (Part B): cd gateway && make build\n4. Bring up the stack (Part C), with --profile redis if you want folder 04's Redis verification to have something to check:\n   docker compose --profile redis up -d gateway-controller gateway-runtime sample-backend redis\n\nIMPORTANT: requests to {{gatewayBaseUrl}} use a self-signed certificate. In Postman, disable 'SSL certificate verification' under Settings > General, or these requests will fail with a TLS error unrelated to the policy itself.\n\nRun folders in order: 00 (health) -> 01 (register) -> 02/03 (test flows) -> 04 (Redis cache verification, optional) -> 05 (cleanup).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "controllerBaseUrl",
      "value": "localhost:9090",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "gateway-controller REST management API, base path /api/management/v1"
    },
    {
      "key": "controllerAdminUrl",
      "value": "localhost:9094",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "gateway-controller admin/health API (port 9094 when using gateway/docker-compose.yaml)"
    },
    {
      "key": "gatewayBaseUrl",
      "value": "localhost:8443",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "gateway-runtime (Envoy) data-plane traffic - self-signed cert, see collection description"
    },
    {
      "key": "imdsMockBaseUrl",
      "value": "localhost:9701",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "mock-azure-imds (run natively on host via go run)"
    },
    {
      "key": "backendBaseUrl",
      "value": "localhost:9602",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "mock-ai-backend, shared with the oauth2 policy's own test harness"
    },
    {
      "key": "adminAuthHeader",
      "value": "Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4=",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "admin:admin"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "00 - Health Checks",
      "description": "Confirm mock-azure-imds, mock-ai-backend, gateway-controller, and gateway-runtime are all up before running anything else.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "mock-azure-imds healthz",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://{{imdsMockBaseUrl}}/healthz",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": [
                "{{imdsMockBaseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "healthz"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "mock-ai-backend healthz",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://{{backendBaseUrl}}/healthz",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": [
                "{{backendBaseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "healthz"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "gateway-controller admin health",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://{{controllerAdminUrl}}/api/admin/v1/health",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": [
                "{{controllerAdminUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "admin",
                "v1",
                "health"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "gateway-runtime reachable (Envoy)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "https://{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/",
              "protocol": "https",
              "host": [
                "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                ""
              ]
            },
            "description": "A 404 here is fine - it just means no route is registered yet."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "01 - Register AI APIs (LLM Providers)",
      "description": "Registers each LlmProvider used by the test flows below. Attached via the generic policies list, not upstream.auth - see TESTING.md Part D.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register: azure-umi-test",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('created (200 or 201)', function () { pm.expect([200, 201]).to.include(pm.response.code); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/yaml"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "{{adminAuthHeader}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://{{controllerBaseUrl}}/api/management/v1/llm-providers",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": [
                "{{controllerBaseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "management",
                "v1",
                "llm-providers"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Happy-path provider for E.1 and E.2 (caching).",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "apiVersion: gateway.api-platform.wso2.com/v1\nkind: LlmProvider\nmetadata:\n  name: azure-umi-test\nspec:\n  displayName: Azure UMI Test\n  version: v1.0\n  template: openai\n  context: /azure-umi-test/latest\n  upstream:\n    url: http://host.docker.internal:9602\n  policies:\n    - name: azure-managed-identity\n      version: v0\n      paths:\n        - path: /chat/completions\n          methods: [POST]\n          params:\n            clientId: 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111\n            resource: https://cognitiveservices.azure.com/\n  accessControl:\n    mode: deny_all\n    exceptions:\n      - path: /chat/completions\n        methods: [POST]\n",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "yaml"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Register: azure-umi-test-broken",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('created (200 or 201)', function () { pm.expect([200, 201]).to.include(pm.response.code); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/yaml"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "{{adminAuthHeader}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://{{controllerBaseUrl}}/api/management/v1/llm-providers",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": [
                "{{controllerBaseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "management",
                "v1",
                "llm-providers"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Simulated IMDS/platform outage for E.3.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "apiVersion: gateway.api-platform.wso2.com/v1\nkind: LlmProvider\nmetadata:\n  name: azure-umi-test-broken\nspec:\n  displayName: Azure UMI Test (simulated platform outage)\n  version: v1.0\n  template: openai\n  context: /azure-umi-test-broken/latest\n  upstream:\n    url: http://host.docker.internal:9602\n  policies:\n    - name: azure-managed-identity\n      version: v0\n      paths:\n        - path: /chat/completions\n          methods: [POST]\n          params:\n            clientId: broken-client\n            resource: https://cognitiveservices.azure.com/\n  accessControl:\n    mode: deny_all\n    exceptions:\n      - path: /chat/completions\n        methods: [POST]\n",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "yaml"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Register: azure-umi-test-malformed",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('created (200 or 201)', function () { pm.expect([200, 201]).to.include(pm.response.code); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/yaml"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "{{adminAuthHeader}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://{{controllerBaseUrl}}/api/management/v1/llm-providers",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": [
                "{{controllerBaseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "management",
                "v1",
                "llm-providers"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Malformed IMDS response (200 OK, missing access_token).",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "apiVersion: gateway.api-platform.wso2.com/v1\nkind: LlmProvider\nmetadata:\n  name: azure-umi-test-malformed\nspec:\n  displayName: Azure UMI Test (malformed IMDS response)\n  version: v1.0\n  template: openai\n  context: /azure-umi-test-malformed/latest\n  upstream:\n    url: http://host.docker.internal:9602\n  policies:\n    - name: azure-managed-identity\n      version: v0\n      paths:\n        - path: /chat/completions\n          methods: [POST]\n          params:\n            clientId: malformed-client\n            resource: https://cognitiveservices.azure.com/\n  accessControl:\n    mode: deny_all\n    exceptions:\n      - path: /chat/completions\n        methods: [POST]\n",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "yaml"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "02 - Mock Debug Endpoints",
      "description": "Inspect/reset mock-azure-imds's request history between test flows.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Reset IMDS stats",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://{{imdsMockBaseUrl}}/debug/reset",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": [
                "{{imdsMockBaseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "debug",
                "reset"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get IMDS stats",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://{{imdsMockBaseUrl}}/debug/stats",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": [
                "{{imdsMockBaseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "debug",
                "stats"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "03 - Test Flows",
      "description": "Run '02 - Reset IMDS stats' before each flow so request counts aren't polluted by earlier ones.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "E.1 - Happy path",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('content shows an injected bearer token', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(json.choices[0].message.content).to.match(/received Authorization: \"Bearer mock-imds-token-/);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "https://{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/azure-umi-test/latest/chat/completions",
              "protocol": "https",
              "host": [
                "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "azure-umi-test",
                "latest",
                "chat",
                "completions"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Expect 200 and choices[0].message.content to read: received Authorization: \"Bearer mock-imds-token-...\". Then check '02 - Get IMDS stats': last history entry should have outcome=issued.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini\", \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"hi\"}]}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "E.2 - Token caching",
          "item": [
            {
              "name": "Send chat request (run x5)",
              "event": [
                {
                  "listen": "test",
                  "script": {
                    "type": "text/javascript",
                    "exec": [
                      "pm.test('status is 200', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              ],
              "request": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [
                  {
                    "key": "Content-Type",
                    "value": "application/json"
                  }
                ],
                "url": {
                  "raw": "https://{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/azure-umi-test/latest/chat/completions",
                  "protocol": "https",
                  "host": [
                    "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}"
                  ],
                  "path": [
                    "azure-umi-test",
                    "latest",
                    "chat",
                    "completions"
                  ]
                },
                "description": "Run this 5 times, then check 'Verify exactly one IMDS call happened' below.",
                "body": {
                  "mode": "raw",
                  "raw": "{\"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini\", \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"hi\"}]}",
                  "options": {
                    "raw": {
                      "language": "json"
                    }
                  }
                }
              },
              "response": []
            },
            {
              "name": "Verify exactly one IMDS call happened",
              "event": [
                {
                  "listen": "test",
                  "script": {
                    "type": "text/javascript",
                    "exec": [
                      "const json = pm.response.json();",
                      "pm.test('tokenRequestCount is 1', function () { pm.expect(json.tokenRequestCount).to.eql(1); });"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              ],
              "request": {
                "method": "GET",
                "header": [],
                "url": {
                  "raw": "http://{{imdsMockBaseUrl}}/debug/stats",
                  "protocol": "http",
                  "host": [
                    "{{imdsMockBaseUrl}}"
                  ],
                  "path": [
                    "debug",
                    "stats"
                  ]
                }
              },
              "response": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "E.3 - Simulated platform outage (expect 502)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 502', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(502); });",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('generic error body', function () { pm.expect(json.message).to.eql('failed to authenticate request to upstream service'); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "https://{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/azure-umi-test-broken/latest/chat/completions",
              "protocol": "https",
              "host": [
                "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "azure-umi-test-broken",
                "latest",
                "chat",
                "completions"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Expect 502 with the generic Bad Gateway body - the underlying 500 from mock-azure-imds must not leak through.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini\", \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"hi\"}]}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "E.4 - Malformed IMDS response (expect 502)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 502', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(502); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "https://{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/azure-umi-test-malformed/latest/chat/completions",
              "protocol": "https",
              "host": [
                "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "azure-umi-test-malformed",
                "latest",
                "chat",
                "completions"
              ]
            },
            "description": "mock-azure-imds returns 200 OK with no access_token - the policy must not crash or forward an empty Authorization header.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini\", \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"hi\"}]}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "04 - Redis Token Cache Verification",
      "description": "Requires the stack to have been started with the redis profile:\n  docker compose --profile redis up -d gateway-controller gateway-runtime sample-backend redis\n\nPostman has no native Redis client, so this folder's real request just populates the cache (same call as E.1) - run the redis-cli commands below yourself afterward, from a terminal:\n\n  docker exec gateway-redis-1 redis-cli KEYS 'azure-managed-identity:token:v1:*'\n  docker exec gateway-redis-1 redis-cli GET '<key>'\n  docker exec gateway-redis-1 redis-cli TTL '<key>'\n\nTo see the fail-open fallback (Redis down doesn't break auth):\n  docker compose stop redis\n  # re-run 'Populate cache' below - still 200 OK, just no longer cached anywhere\n  docker compose start redis",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Populate cache (send chat request)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "https://{{gatewayBaseUrl}}/azure-umi-test/latest/chat/completions",
              "protocol": "https",
              "host": [
                "{{gatewayBaseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "azure-umi-test",
                "latest",
                "chat",
                "completions"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Same request as E.1 - run this first so there's a fresh token to find in Redis. Requires 'Register: azure-umi-test' (folder 01) to have been run already.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini\", \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"hi\"}]}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "05 - Cleanup",
      "description": "Deletes all test LlmProviders. Run once you're done, or skip and just docker compose down -v.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Delete: azure-umi-test",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "{{adminAuthHeader}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://{{controllerBaseUrl}}/api/management/v1/llm-providers/azure-umi-test",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": [
                "{{controllerBaseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "management",
                "v1",
                "llm-providers",
                "azure-umi-test"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete: azure-umi-test-broken",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "{{adminAuthHeader}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://{{controllerBaseUrl}}/api/management/v1/llm-providers/azure-umi-test-broken",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": [
                "{{controllerBaseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "management",
                "v1",
                "llm-providers",
                "azure-umi-test-broken"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete: azure-umi-test-malformed",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
